"""Game Mode: a one-click front end for this machine's CPU reservation.

Deployed to /usr/local/bin/game-mode. See README.md.

This is a front end. Every change to the machine belongs to game-mode-cpus,
which this program shells out to; if a toggle fails, its own words are what
the user sees. The live picture reads /proc/stat and cgroup cpu.stat
directly, because those are read-only and cheap.

Run with --self-test to build every page and draw every state once.
"""

